invariant: INV-74
file: src/tcp_seal.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: ch_seal_in_place seals each record where the run of plaintext
  left it, without moving the plaintext of record i forward by i *
  REC_OVERHEAD bytes, so every record after the first seals the bytes of
  the record before it and the header and tag of that record. The peer
  reads other plaintext than the caller wrote (docs/decisions.md 248).

--- old
        if (i > 0) {
            memmove(rec + REC_HDR, buf + i * layout->limit + REC_HDR, len);
        }
--- new
